[?2004l[?1049h[22;0;0t[40;1H[?1h=[4mTMUX[24m(1)                                General Commands Manual                              [4mTMUX[24m(1)[m
[m
[1mNAME[0m[m
       tmux — terminal multiplexer[m
[m
[1mSYNOPSIS[0m[m
       [1mtmux   [22m[[1m-2CDlNuVv[22m]   [[1m-c   [4m[22mshell-command[24m]   [[1m-f  [4m[22mfile[24m]  [[1m-L  [4m[22msocket-name[24m]  [[1m-S  [4m[22msocket-path[24m][m
            [[1m-T [4m[22mfeatures[24m] [[4mcommand[24m [[4mflags[24m]][m
[m
[1mDESCRIPTION[0m[m
       [1mtmux [22mis a terminal multiplexer: it enables a number of terminals to  be  created,  accessed,[m
       and  controlled  from a single screen.  [1mtmux [22mmay be detached from a screen and continue run‐[m
       ning in the background, then later reattached.[m
[m
       When [1mtmux [22mis started, it creates a new [4msession[24m with a  single  [4mwindow[24m  and  displays  it  on[m
       screen.   A status line at the bottom of the screen shows information on the current session[m
       and is used to enter interactive commands.[m
[m
       A session is a single collection of [4mpseudo[24m [4mterminals[24m under the  management  of  [1mtmux[22m.   Each[m
       session  has  one or more windows linked to it.  A window occupies the entire screen and may[m
       be split into rectangular panes, each of which is a separate  pseudo  terminal  (the  [4mpty[24m(4)[m
       manual  page  documents  the technical details of pseudo terminals).  Any number of [1mtmux [22min‐[m
       stances may connect to the same session, and any number of windows may  be  present  in  the[m
       same session.  Once all sessions are killed, [1mtmux [22mexits.[m
[m
       Each session is persistent and will survive accidental disconnection (such as [4mssh[24m(1) connec‐[m
       tion  timeout)  or  intentional detaching (with the ‘C-b d’ key strokes).  [1mtmux [22mmay be reat‐[m
       tached using:[m
[m
             [1m$ tmux attach[0m[m
[m
       In [1mtmux[22m, a session is displayed on screen by a [4mclient[24m and all sessions are managed by a sin‐[m
       gle [4mserver[24m.  The server and each client are separate processes which communicate  through  a[m
       socket in [4m/tmp[24m.[m
[m
       The options are as follows:[m
[m
       [1m-2            [22mForce [1mtmux [22mto assume the terminal supports 256 colours.  This is equivalent to[m
                     [1m-T [4m[22m256[24m.[m
[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
       [1m-C            [22mStart  in  control  mode  (see the “CONTROL MODE” section).  Given twice ([1m-CC[22m)[m
                     disables echo.[m
[m
       [1m-c [4m[22mshell-command[0m[m
                     Execute [4mshell-command[24m using the default shell.  If necessary, the [1mtmux  [22mserver[m
                     will be started to retrieve the [1mdefault-shell [22moption.  This option is for com‐[m
                     patibility with [4msh[24m(1) when [1mtmux [22mis used as a login shell.[m
[m
       [1m-D            [22mDo  not start the [1mtmux [22mserver as a daemon.  This also turns the [1mexit-empty [22mop‐[m
                     tion off.  With [1m-D[22m, [4mcommand[24m may not be specified.[m
[m
       [1m-f [4m[22mfile[24m       Specify an alternative configuration file.  By default, [1mtmux [22mloads the  system[m
                     configuration file from [4m/etc/tmux.conf[24m, if present, then looks for a user con‐[m
                     figuration file at [4m~/.tmux.conf[24m or [4m$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tmux/tmux.conf[24m.[m
[m
                     The  configuration  file  is  a set of [1mtmux [22mcommands which are executed in se‐[m
                     quence when the server is first started.  [1mtmux [22mloads configuration files  once[m
                     when  the  server process has started.  The [1msource-file [22mcommand may be used to[m
                     load a file later.[m
[m
                     [1mtmux [22mshows any error messages from commands  in  configuration  files  in  the[m
                     first  session created, and continues to process the rest of the configuration[m
                     file.[m
[m
       [1m-L [4m[22msocket-name[0m[m
                     [1mtmux [22mstores the server socket in a directory under TMUX_TMPDIR or [4m/tmp[24m  if  it[m
                     is  unset.  The default socket is named [4mdefault[24m.  This option allows a differ‐[m
                     ent socket name to be specified, allowing several independent [1mtmux [22mservers  to[m
                     be  run.   Unlike [1m-S [22ma full path is not necessary: the sockets are all created[m
                     in a directory [4mtmux-UID[24m under the directory given by TMUX_TMPDIR or  in  [4m/tmp[24m.[m
                     The  [4mtmux-UID[24m  directory  is  created  by [1mtmux [22mand must not be world readable,[m
                     writable or executable.[m
[m
                     If the socket is accidentally removed, the SIGUSR1 signal may be sent  to  the[m
                     [1mtmux [22mserver process to recreate it (note that this will fail if any parent di‐[m
                     rectories are missing).[m
[m
